# Glob, not one literal per destination: ci.yml writes a result bundle per
# test leg (TestResults.xcresult, TestResults-ipad.xcresult), and any one of
# them left untracked makes `git status --porcelain` non-empty, which is
# exactly what Scripts/check-red-green.sh refuses to run against. Adding a
# destination must not silently turn TEST_PROOF into `error` on every pull
# request. See docs/learnings/fixture-stub-trips-own-dirty-tree-guard.md.
TestResults*.xcresult
.testflight-feedback-seen
.superpowers/
